---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../../consts';
import { getInsightBySlug, buildArticleJsonLd } from '../../../data/insights';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const post = getInsightBySlug('founder-story')!;
const articleJsonLd = buildArticleJsonLd(post, SITE.url);
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Dr. Hemant L. Patel — 18+ Years of Public Health Leadership | Causewave"
  description={post.description}
  ogTitle="Dr. Hemant L. Patel | Public Health & CSR Leadership"
  ogDescription="18+ years driving government engagement, evidence-based program scale-up, and digital public health innovation across WHO, CARE India, and Government of Gujarat."
  canonicalPath={post.path}
  activePage="insights"
  ogType="article"
  breadcrumbLabel={post.shortTitle}
  breadcrumbParent={{ name: 'Insights', path: 'insights/' }}
  jsonLd={articleJsonLd}
>
  <main>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="bg-slate-900 text-white section">
      <div class="max-w-screen-2xl mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <a href={`${base}insights/`} class="inline-flex items-center text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors mb-6">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
            Back to Insights
          </a>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="text-xs font-medium text-amber-400 bg-amber-400/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full">Founder Story</span>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500">2026</span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Dr. Hemant L. Patel — 18+ Years of Public Health Impact</h1>
          <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300 text-lg">From designing Gujarat's award-winning last-mile healthcare models to enabling India's highest single-day vaccination drive — the journey behind Causewave.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Article Content -->
    <article class="section max-w-screen-2xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">

        <!-- Quick facts -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3 mb-10">
          <div class="bg-white border p-4 rounded-xl text-center">
            <div class="text-xl font-bold text-sky-600">18+</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600">Years in Public Health</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border p-4 rounded-xl text-center">
            <div class="text-xl font-bold text-teal-600">33 Lakh+</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600">Single-Day Vaccinations</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border p-4 rounded-xl text-center">
            <div class="text-xl font-bold text-emerald-600">SKOCH</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600">Gold Award</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border p-4 rounded-xl text-center">
            <div class="text-xl font-bold text-sky-600">30+</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600">Outbreaks Detected</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">The Beginning: Gujarat's Frontline</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Dr. Hemant L. Patel began his career where public health matters most — on the ground. As Municipal Health Officer in Kalol, Gandhinagar, he led urban public health governance, epidemic control, sanitation, and National Urban Health Mission implementation for the city.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Under his leadership, Kalol achieved Open Defecation Free (ODF) certification and earned the 34th national ranking and 4th Gujarat ranking under the Swachh Bharat Mission. He designed epidemic-prevention systems based on local disease trends, led high-performing family planning initiatives recognized by the district administration, and supported the introduction of new vaccines including Pentavalent, MR-2, and IPV.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">WHO Sitamarhi: Surveillance That Saved Lives</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          In December 2017, Dr. Patel joined the World Health Organization as Surveillance Medical Officer in Sitamarhi — one of India's Aspirational Districts. His work here would demonstrate the life-saving power of systematic data.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          He strengthened surveillance systems that identified <strong>30+ measles outbreaks (20+ lab-confirmed)</strong> from a zero-detection baseline — an achievement that fundamentally shifted Sitamarhi from outbreak-based to case-based surveillance, supporting national measles elimination goals.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          He prepared the Health Action Plan for Sitamarhi Aspirational District presented to the Government of India, and led the extended Gram Swaraj Abhiyan achieving one of the highest child immunization numbers in the state and nation. He also supported the introduction of new vaccines — PCV, Rotavirus, JE, and MR — during major campaigns despite elections, exams, and human resource constraints.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Bihar COVID-19 Maha-Abhiyan: 33 Lakh Vaccinations in One Day</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          When COVID-19 struck, Dr. Patel was serving on the Bihar State CORE Team for COVID-19 surveillance and vaccination through CARE India. He provided chief-of-staff-style support to senior leadership — managing daily and weekly reviews, operational briefs, dashboards, action tracking, partner alignment, and escalation across governance rhythms.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The result was historic: <strong>Bihar achieved 33+ lakh vaccinations in a single day</strong> — the highest in India. Dr. Patel was felicitated by the Health Minister of Bihar for this achievement.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          His vaccine distribution analytics and digital reporting systems — including dashboards, chatbot workflows, and EHR-linked tools — reduced district-level coverage variation from ±20% to approximately 5%, enabling more equitable access across the state.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Gujarat's Chitta Express: Last-Mile Innovation That Won a National Award</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Dr. Patel designed and operationalized the Chitta/Cheetah Bike Express and Sanjeevani Express — last-mile delivery models that brought healthcare to hard-to-reach populations in Gujarat's tribal and remote areas.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The models were adopted by the Government of Gujarat and replicated across districts. The innovation earned the <strong>SKOCH Gold Award</strong> and was featured as a <strong>case study at IIM Raipur</strong> — recognition of a model that proved last-mile healthcare delivery doesn't have to be expensive or complex to work.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Dr. Patel's approach was grounded in data: analytics-driven dashboards that visualized coverage gaps in real time, enabling rapid course-correction and ensuring no community was left behind.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">CARE India: Multi-State Expansion Across 11 States</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          At CARE India, Dr. Patel provided backend support to 11 states and took leadership roles in Bihar, Jharkhand, Manipur, and Gujarat. His skill was converting concepts into government-supported implementation pathways — bridging the gap between program design and what actually works on the ground.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          He also led Teekanama, a monthly immunization knowledge product curating state progress, best practices, and implementation learnings for government and partner stakeholders.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          As Head of Immunization Division, he represented CARE India in national and state coordination forums with the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, National Health Mission, WHO, UNICEF, and the State Health Society Bihar.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Digital Health & AI: Building for Scale</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Recognizing the power of technology to transform public health, Dr. Patel founded Sankhyank Tech Solutions — a health-tech venture delivering digital public health tools, analytics platforms, AI-enabled workflows, and data transformation solutions for government and NGO decision-making.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          His digital health work includes dashboards, automated reporting, cloud-based reporting systems, Meta/Facebook-linked COVID-19 vaccination chatbot workflows, and ABDM-aligned tool development. He coordinated AI-enabled production of 100+ minutes of frontline health worker training content under a World Bank-funded Gujarat project.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          At WISH Foundation, he led program strategy and digital health initiatives, guiding ABDM-aligned tool development for scalable implementation.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">International Recognition</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Dr. Patel was a speaker at <strong>Biologistics World Asia 2021</strong>, presenting on COVID-19 vaccine rollout, cold chain management, and immunization supply chains — sharing lessons from India's vaccination experience with an international audience.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Why This Matters for CSR</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Causewave was founded on the belief that CSR programs should deliver both compliance and real community impact. Dr. Patel's 18+ years across WHO, CARE India, Government of Gujarat, and health-tech entrepreneurship mean Causewave doesn't just advise — it implements. The same rigor that reduced vaccination coverage gaps from ±20% to 5%, that detected 30+ outbreaks from zero, that scaled a bike-based healthcare model to a national award — that's the expertise behind every CSR engagement.
        </p>

        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Continue exploring Causewave’s practical guides:
          <a href={`${base}insights/csr-compliance-companies-act-2013/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">CSR compliance under the Companies Act 2013</a>,
          <a href={`${base}insights/impactful-csr-programs-healthcare/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">healthcare CSR design</a>, and
          <a href={`${base}insights/measuring-csr-impact-framework/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">impact measurement</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 border">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Want to work with Dr. Patel and the Causewave team?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">18+ years of public health leadership, now available for your CSR programs. Explore <a href={`${base}services/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">services</a> or get in touch.</p>
          <a href={`${base}contact/`} class="mt-4 inline-flex btn btn-primary px-6 py-2 text-sm">Get in Touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
